config BR2_PACKAGE_XEN_GUEST_EXT
	bool "xen-guest"
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_BUSYBOX
	help
	  A small Linux guest for the Xen tests, in /opt/xen-guest: a
	  kernel built for a Xen PV-console guest (Xen guest support,
	  hvc0, the FF-A transport and the OP-TEE driver, so a guest
	  given a TEE by its toolstack can reach it) and an initramfs
	  with BusyBox. The guest's init prints a ready line and a TEE
	  line on hvc0, stays up, and prints a poweroff line when the
	  toolstack asks it to shut down (the console protocol of the
	  test-definitions automated/linux/xen README).
